.\" Adapted for BNU from the GNU Coreutils 9.11 manual page; see doc/README.md.
.TH TEE "1" "2026-07-28" "BNU 9.11" "BNU Commands"
.SH NAME
tee \- read from standard input and write to standard output and files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tee
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR]... [\fI\,FILE\/\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" This page is derived from GNU Coreutils documentation.
This page documents BNU, an independent Bun implementation compatible with
GNU Coreutils 9.11.
.PP
Copy standard input to each FILE, and also to standard output.
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#tee-a'\fB\-a, \-\-append\fP\X'tty: link'
append to the given FILEs, do not overwrite
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#tee-i'\fB\-i, \-\-ignore\-interrupts\fP\X'tty: link'
ignore interrupt signals
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#tee-p'\fB\-p\fP\X'tty: link'
operate in a more appropriate MODE with pipes
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#tee--output-error'\fB\-\-output\-error[=MODE]\fP\X'tty: link'
set behavior on write error.  See MODE below
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/tee#tee--help'\fB\-\-help\fP\X'tty: link'
display this help and exit
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/tee#tee--version'\fB\-\-version\fP\X'tty: link'
output version information and exit
.SS "MODE determines behavior with write errors on the outputs:"
.TP
warn
diagnose errors writing to any output
.TP
warn\-nopipe
diagnose errors writing to any output not a pipe
.TP
exit
exit on error writing to any output
.TP
exit\-nopipe
exit on error writing to any output not a pipe
.PP
The default MODE for the \fB\-p\fR option is 'warn\-nopipe'.
With "nopipe" MODEs, exit immediately if all outputs become broken pipes.
The default operation when \fB\-\-output\-error\fR is not specified, is to
exit immediately on error writing to a pipe, and diagnose errors
writing to non pipe outputs.
